  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "visit, call",
      "explanation": "The act of someone coming to visit a place or person. A formal word used when describing visitors arriving, especially in business, official, or polite contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "13120_raihou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{来訪者|らいほうしゃ}は{受付|うけつけ}へどうぞ。",
      "english": "Visitors, please proceed to the reception desk.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13120_raihou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{大臣|だいじん}が{来訪|らいほう}する{予定|よてい}だ。",
      "english": "The minister is scheduled to visit.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13120_raihou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{海外|かいがい}からの{来訪者|らいほうしゃ}を{迎|むか}えるために、{準備|じゅんび}を{進|すす}めている。",
      "english": "We are making preparations to welcome visitors from overseas.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {来訪者|らいほうしゃ}: visitor, caller\n- {来訪|らいほう}する: to visit, to call on\n- {来訪|らいほう}を{受|う}ける: to receive a visit\n\nUSAGE:\n{来訪|らいほう} is a formal word. It describes the visit from the perspective of the person or place being visited (someone comes to you). For casual visits, {訪問|ほうもん} (visiting someone) or simply {来|く}る is more common.",
